---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /resources/
title: Resources
description: "Field notes on finding and winning B2B customers: how to pick who to approach, how to disqualify fast, and what to actually send the ones who are left."
---

<header class="res-hub-hero">
  <div class="res-hub-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">resources</span>
    <h1 class="res-hub-h1">How to find customers worth having — and what to send them</h1>
    <p class="res-hub-lede">
      Most prospecting advice stops at the list. The hard half is the other one:
      what goes in the email once you know who you are writing to. These are field
      notes on both, written from teardowns of real businesses with real numbers on
      the table — not from a keyword tool.
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="res-hub">
  {% set articles = collections.resources | related('', 999) %}
  {% if articles.length %}
  {#- The filter row is derived from the articles by the `topics` filter, and
      ships hidden: resources.js is what reveals it, so a reader without JS gets
      the whole list instead of buttons that do nothing (#159). -#}
  {#- A div, not a <nav>: main.css styles the bare `nav` element as the site's
      fixed header, so a <nav> here gets pinned over the logo. This is a group of
      toggle buttons rather than site navigation anyway. -#}
  <div class="res-filter" role="group" data-topic-filter hidden aria-label="Filter articles by topic">
    <button type="button" class="res-chip is-on" data-filter="" aria-pressed="true">Everything</button>
    {%- for t in collections.resources | topics %}
    <button type="button" class="res-chip" data-filter="{{ t.topic }}" aria-pressed="false">{{ t.topic }} <span class="res-chip-n">{{ t.count }}</span></button>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
  <p class="res-filter-count" data-filter-count aria-live="polite"></p>
  <ul class="res-grid" data-article-grid>
    {%- for a in articles %}
    <li class="res-card" data-topic="{{ a.data.topic or "lead generation" }}">
      <a href="{{ a.url }}">
        <span class="res-card-topic">{{ a.data.topic or "lead generation" }}</span>
        <h2 class="res-card-title">{{ a.data.title }}</h2>
        <p class="res-card-dek">{{ a.data.dek or a.data.description }}</p>
        <span class="res-card-meta">
          <time datetime="{{ a.data.date | isoDate }}">{{ a.data.date | readableDate }}</time>
          {% if a.data.readingTime %}<span class="res-dot">·</span>{{ a.data.readingTime }} min read{% endif %}
        </span>
      </a>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% else %}
  <p class="res-empty">The first articles are being written. Come back shortly.</p>
  {% endif %}
</section>

<section class="res-hub-cta">
  <div class="res-hub-cta-inner">
    <span class="tag">try it</span>
    <h2>Stop reading. Point it at your own company.</h2>
    <p>Prospektor reads a company's own website before it says a word about them,
      scores partnership fit against what you are actually hunting for, and drafts
      the deck, the emails and the call prep in your voice. The scan is free.</p>
    <a class="btn-cta" href="/#scan">Scan your site</a>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="{{ '/assets/js/resources.js' | asset }}" defer></script>
